  "faris/pr-by-subsidiary": {
    "description": "Заявки на закупку по восьми дочкам холдинга Al-Faris — кто генерирует объём очереди.",
    "help": "<!-- compose-help:v2 -->\n# Purchase requests by subsidiary\n\nDoughnut of purchase requests by subsidiary_code. Shows which of the eight operating companies generates PR volume — not which one spends the most SAR (that is the spend-by-subsidiary bar).\n\nA silent company on this ring with live ERP budget lines means they are not raising requests, or the code on the PR does not match the subsidiary master. A dominant slice is not automatically “bad”: it may be the largest entity. Compare with cycle time and stalled count on the group dashboard: volume without stalls is healthy; volume plus overdue is a governance problem.\n\nEmpty ring means no PRs or a page filter. Drill into the register. Codes must stay stable — renaming a subsidiary code will split history across two slices. Amounts stay on the spend charts; this one is ticket count."
  },
